parameters.text:
You are reviewing raw smartphone footage for a short-form vertical video (Reel).

Score candidate segments using these rules:
KEEP: subject in focus and camera fairly steady; clear action, movement, reaction or reveal; faces visible and well lit; clean audio when someone speaks; strong opening moment usable as a hook.
REJECT: camera pointing at floor/pocket/sky; heavy shake or blur; several seconds with nothing changing; too dark or overexposed.
Also decide framing for a vertical 9:16 Reel. Use "crop" only if the main subject is one person or object in the CENTER of the frame (e.g. someone talking straight to camera). Use "pad" for everything else: screen recordings, slides, a person in a corner or webcam window, an off-center subject, or action spread across the frame. If unsure, use "pad".

Return 1 to 5 segments, each 3 to 15 seconds long. If nothing in the video is usable, return an empty segments list and explain why in "summary".

Respond with JSON only, no other text, in exactly this shape:
{
  "summary": "one sentence describing the video",
  "usable": true,
  "segments": [
    { "start": 4.0, "end": 11.5, "score": 8, "reason": "short reason", "hook_candidate": true }
  ]
}
{
  "summary": "one sentence describing the video",
  "usable": true,
  "framing": "crop",
  "segments": [ ... ]
}

